  "notes": [
    "The course map prints only course codes, prerequisites, a category colour per course and per-semester credit totals (9, 11, 13, 10, 13, 12, 10, 10, 9, 10, '06/09', '07/04'). It prints no degree total, no version/effective year (version 'Course Map', effectiveFromYear 0), no course titles and no per-course credits.",
    "totalCredits 120 is inferred, not printed: semesters 1-10 = 107, and the printed alternatives for semesters 11-12 ('06/09' and '07/04') both add 13 more, giving 120 either way.",
    "Per-course credits are inferred from the semester totals: theory courses 3, lab ('L') courses 1, BBT422 4 (semester 12 drops from 7 to 4 when BBT426 is not taken, so BBT422 = 4 and BBT426 = 3). Every printed semester total matches.",
    "Electives: the map places all seven elective/free elective courses (BBT418, 419, 421, 423, 425, 426, 427) in semesters 8-12; notes say at least 3 must be taken as electives and 3 free electives are encouraged from the same list. Modelled as 3 Elective rows at the map's first three elective positions (BBT423 sem 8, BBT419 sem 9, BBT418 sem 10), each listing the other six as alternatives, plus FREE-ELECT1-3 (two in sem 11, one in sem 12, matching the '06' and '07' totals). Prerequisites of the alternatives are not representable: BBT421 needs BBT316+BBT317, BBT425 needs BBT417, BBT427 needs BBT415, BBT426 needs CHE203+BBT335.",
    "Categories are the printed colour legend: Univ. GED (green), SHLS/School Core (blue), Major Required (red), Elective/Free Elective (magenta).",
    "English: 'ENG102/ENG103*' (sem 1) -> ENG102 with alternative ENG103; 'ENG103/ENG105*' (sem 2, prerequisite 'ENG102/ENG103') -> ENG103 with alternative ENG105; the printed prerequisite 'ENG102/ENG103' is not stored, because ENG103 cannot be its own prerequisite and the slot is already filled by either code. Map notes: ENG103 only if ENG102 is waived or completed; ENG103 & ENG105 are mandatory for all NSU UG students; batch 152-162 students waived in ENG102 must take ENG111.",
    "BEN205 and HIS103 are marked mandatory from batch 163 onwards; batch 152-162 may take any of HIS101/HIS102/HIS103 instead.",
    "'POL101/POL104/ECO101/ECO104/SOC101/ANT101/' is one slot (trailing slash as printed).",
    "Titles are not printed. Titles were taken from other NSU sources in the same download set: BIO103/BIO201 'Principles of Biology I/II', CHE101/CHE201 'General Chemistry I/II', CHE202 'Organic Chemistry I', BBT230, BBT315, BBT318, BBT413, BBT418, BBT419 (older BS in Microbiology document, may be outdated), ENG/BEN/HIS/POL/ECO/SOC/ANT/MAT from other maps. Lab titles are derived from their theory course. Remaining titles are '(title not printed)'.",
    "MAT116 counts 3 credits here (needed for the 11-credit semester 2)."
  ],
